# Source vs generated

This is a static site. GitHub Actions runs `npm ci` + `npm run build` and deploys `dist/`.

- Edit `components/`, `assets/`, `build/template.html`, `build/build.js`. Never edit `dist/`.
- Preview with `npm run build` (or `npm start`). Do not commit `dist/`, `vendor/`, `cache/`, `node_modules/`, or `.DS_Store`.
- `theme/` and `bootstrap/` are unmodified third-party. Site-specific CSS/JS goes in `assets/` or `components/<section>/`.
- `vendor/` is gitignored but some files are still historically tracked — do not add more vendor files.
- Live sections are whatever is in `build/template.html` nav + `COMPONENTS` in `build/build.js`. **NYC is WIP** (not wired). **Gallery** is built but the nav link and `<!--@include:gallery-->` stay commented out — do not re-enable or delete either unless asked (inlining it would download tens of MB of photos on every visit).
- URLs are paths (`/about/`, `/dining/michelin/`), not hashes. `build.js` copies `index.html` into each route folder so GitHub Pages refresh works.
- Resume: GPA only, no semester grades.
- **Private tabs** (Daily Devotion, Hotel Collection): the live site only ships AES-GCM envelopes from `components/gated/`. Do not copy `devotions.json`, `hotels.json`, `hotel-visits.json`, or `components/travel/img/visits/` into `dist/`. Never commit the unlock passphrase (use `GATE_PASSWORD` or a gitignored `.env`). After editing plaintext, run `npm run gate-encrypt` and commit the updated `components/gated/*` files only.
